  "nl_text": "The rschema_0461 database is designed to manage a retail business, storing information about products, customers, orders, and delivery personnel. The Product table contains details about the items sold, including their category, description, location, name, product ID, stock quantity, unit price, and unit of measurement. The Delivery_Personnel table stores information about the individuals responsible for delivering products, with fields for their ID, gender, name, phone number, and position. The Customer table holds data about the individuals or businesses making purchases, including their address, age, ID, gender, name, and phone number. The Order table tracks customer transactions, with fields for the customer's ID, delivery address, order creation time, order number, status, and total price, referencing the Customer table for the customer's ID. The Order_Product table links orders to the products they contain, with fields for the order ID, product ID, and quantity, referencing both the Order and Product tables. The Order_Delivery table manages the delivery process, with fields for the delivery personnel's ID, estimated delivery time, and order ID, referencing both the Delivery_Personnel and Order tables.",
  "gold_question": "The system is a product distribution center information management system. In terms of product management, the system maintains detailed information for each product, including Product ID, Name, Unit Price, Stock Quantity, Unit of Measurement, Category, Description, and Storage Location. In terms of distribution personnel management, the system records basic information for each distribution personnel, including Delivery Personnel ID, Name, Phone, Gender, and Position, to facilitate personnel scheduling. In terms of customer management, the system maintains basic information for customers, including Customer ID, Name, Gender, Age, Phone, and Address, ensuring accurate processing and delivery of orders. In terms of order management, the system records complete information for each order, including Customer ID, Product ID, Order Creation Time, Product Quantity, Total Order Price, Delivery Address, Order Status, Estimated Delivery Time, and Responsible Delivery Personnel ID, enabling comprehensive tracking and management of the order process. Through the collaborative operation of these functional modules, the system achieves precise management of product inventory, automation of order processing, and real-time monitoring of the delivery process.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0461.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0461\nCREATE TABLE `product` (\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `category` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stock_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `unit_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `unit_of_measurement` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`product_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `delivery_personnel` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `position` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `customer` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `age` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `order` (\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `delivery_address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `order_creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `order_number` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `total_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `order_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `order_product` (\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_id`, `product_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `order_product_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`order_id`) REFERENCES `order` (`order_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `order_product_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `product` (`product_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `order_delivery` (\n  `delivery_personnel_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `estimated_delivery_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`delivery_personnel_id`, `order_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `order_delivery_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`delivery_personnel_id`) REFERENCES `delivery_personnel` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `order_delivery_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`order_id`) REFERENCES `order` (`order_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
